  <!-- BACKGROUND -->
  <ShowcaseSection label="Background" heading="Background">
    <p>A travel agency running memberships and bookings, handling billing, membership records, and day-to-day customer messaging — mostly over WhatsApp — alongside the usual internal tools a small team ends up juggling logins for. Two separate pieces of work came out of that: an automation suite handling the repetitive parts, and two purpose-built systems for the team itself.</p>
  </ShowcaseSection>

  <!-- THE AUTOMATION SUITE — descriptive only, no numbers, per copy -->
  <ShowcaseSection label="The Automation Suite" heading="What Was Built — The Automation Suite">
    <p>Billing emails flow into a spreadsheet automatically. Membership records update as part of the same flow. WhatsApp messages — member welcomes, membership updates — go out without someone typing each one by hand. This piece of the work runs through automation behind the scenes, so no volumes are cited for it here — only what it does.</p>
  </ShowcaseSection>

  <!-- THE SYSTEMS -->
  <ShowcaseSection label="The Systems" heading="What Was Built — The Systems" accent="gold">
    <p><strong>An internal tools portal.</strong> One login, one dashboard, every internal tool behind it — links to other systems, embedded views of internal services, a chat interface that proxies messages to the automation layer, and a document tool that takes a travel itinerary as a Word document, sends it through an AI rewrite step, and hands back a rebuilt version with its formatting intact. Built in about a week.</p>
    <p><strong>A WhatsApp inbox, built from scratch.</strong> Not a wrapper around an existing WhatsApp product — a purpose-built, agent-facing inbox on top of Meta's own WhatsApp Cloud API, with its own database as the single source of truth for every conversation. Handles WhatsApp's 24-hour session window, sends template messages once that window closes, stores inbound and outbound media, and includes an automated activity log recording what an automation workflow did, whether it succeeded, and its estimated cost. Built over about two months.</p>
  </ShowcaseSection>

  <!-- HARDEST PROBLEM -->
  <ShowcaseSection label="The Hardest Problem" heading="Rewriting a Travel Itinerary Document With AI, Without Breaking It">
    <p>One tool in the internal portal takes a real travel itinerary — a Word document, not plain text — and needs to hand it to an AI step for rewriting without losing its formatting. The fix: the document's text gets extracted, sent off for rewriting, and rebuilt back into a proper Word document afterward — rather than round-tripping through plain text and losing the original structure.</p>
  </ShowcaseSection>

  <!-- INTEGRATIONS -->
  <ShowcaseSection label="Integrations" heading="Integrations">
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Meta WhatsApp Cloud API</strong> for the WhatsApp inbox — sending and receiving text, images, and template messages directly, no third-party WhatsApp wrapper.</li>
      <li><strong>n8n</strong>, used two ways: receiving inbound WhatsApp messages and logging them into the inbox's own records, and running the automation suite (billing-email intake, membership updates, outbound WhatsApp messages) as a separate workflow layer outside these two systems.</li>
      <li>An internal chat/automation proxy inside the tools portal, so staff can trigger the same automation layer from inside the portal itself.</li>
    </ul>
  </ShowcaseSection>

  <!-- RESULTS — qualitative, not numeric, so rendered as narrative rather than forced into the results-table shape -->
  <ShowcaseSection label="Results" heading="Results">
    <ul>
      <li>Billing emails get filed automatically instead of retyped by hand.</li>
      <li>Membership records update themselves as part of the same flow.</li>
      <li>WhatsApp welcomes and membership updates go out on their own, not one at a time.</li>
      <li>Every internal staff tool sits behind a single login instead of scattered logins and bookmarks.</li>
      <li>Travel itinerary documents get rewritten by AI with their formatting kept intact.</li>
      <li>Every customer conversation is stored in the agency's own system, not scattered across apps and phones.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>What wasn't measured: message volume, billing-email throughput, and membership-update counts aren't part of this case study — those run through automation behind the scenes and weren't tracked as figures.</p>
  </ShowcaseSection>

